Mwangaza Hardware Website — Legal Compliance Checklist

Status: Draft
Business owner approval: Pending
Last reviewed: 2026-10-29

1. Business authorization

- [ ] Obtain the owner's written approval to build and publish the website.
- [ ] Confirm the business's legal name and authorized contact details.
- [ ] Obtain approval to use the business name, logo, photographs and product information.
- [ ] Agree on the marketing agency's responsibilities in writing.
- [ ] Agree on commission calculation, attribution, reconciliation and payout terms before commission activity begins.

2. Privacy and personal data

- [ ] Identify every personal-data field collected and why it is needed.
- [ ] Identify where enquiries and customer records will be stored.
- [ ] Document who can access customer information.
- [ ] Draft and review "PRIVACY_POLICY.md".
- [ ] Define data retention, deletion, security and incident-response procedures.
- [ ] Establish a process for handling privacy requests and complaints.
- [ ] Assess applicable Kenyan data-protection obligations, including any registration requirements.
- [ ] Review third-party services, analytics, hosting and WhatsApp integrations before enabling them.

3. Website terms and customer protection

- [ ] Draft and review "TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS.md".
- [ ] Verify product descriptions, prices and availability before publication.
- [ ] Clearly distinguish estimates, quotations, confirmed orders and completed payments.
- [ ] Document delivery, collection, cancellations, returns, refunds and complaint procedures.
- [ ] Draft "RETURNS_REFUNDS_AND_CANCELLATIONS.md" to reflect approved store policy and applicable law.
- [ ] Ensure customer-facing claims are accurate and not misleading.

4. Cookies, analytics and marketing

- [ ] Document analytics and tracking technologies used.
- [ ] Draft "COOKIE_AND_ANALYTICS_NOTICE.md" where applicable.
- [ ] Review consent and opt-out requirements before enabling tracking or marketing.
- [ ] Keep promotional communications separate from messages needed to answer customer enquiries.
- [ ] Verify authorization and provider requirements before enabling WhatsApp automation.

5. Payments and financial controls — future phase

- [ ] Obtain owner approval before enabling payment collection.
- [ ] Verify the authorized business payment account and payment provider.
- [ ] Document transaction confirmation, reconciliation, refunds and dispute handling.
- [ ] Keep payment credentials and provider secrets out of public code.
- [ ] Test payment failures, duplicate notifications and refunds before launch.
- [ ] Finalize the written agency and commission agreement before calculating or paying commission.

6. Launch approval

- [ ] Review the applicable legal requirements with a qualified Kenyan professional where needed.
- [ ] Verify all business details and approved policies.
- [ ] Test privacy notices, forms, consent choices and complaint channels.
- [ ] Confirm no unapproved customer-data collection or live payments are enabled.
- [ ] Record owner approval and outstanding risks before public launch.

Status definitions

- Not started: Work has not begun.
- In progress: Work is underway.
- Verified: Evidence has been checked and recorded.
- Requires legal review: A qualified professional or relevant authority must clarify the requirement.

Rule: Do not mark a requirement Verified without evidence. This checklist does not itself establish legal compliance.
